{"id":136,"name":"flareon","speciesId":136,"dex":136,"form":"normal","generation":1,"types":["fire"],"stats":{"hp":65,"attack":130,"defense":60,"special-attack":95,"special-defense":110,"speed":65},"abilities":[{"name":"flash-fire","hidden":false},{"name":"guts","hidden":true}],"height":9,"weight":250,"baseExp":184,"sprites":{"normal":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/136.png","shiny":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/shiny/136.png","icon":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/136.png"},"cry":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/cries/main/cries/pokemon/latest/136.ogg","genus":"Flame Pokémon","genusPt":"Pokémon Flamejante","flavor":[{"version":"red","text":"When storing thermal energy in its body, its temperature could soar to over 1600 degrees."},{"version":"yellow","text":"It has a flame chamber inside its body. It inhales, then blows out fire that is over 3,000F degrees."},{"version":"gold","text":"It stores some of the air it inhales in its internal flame pouch, which heats it to over 3,000 degrees."},{"version":"silver","text":"It fluffs out its fur collar to cool down its body temperature, which can reach 1,650 degrees."},{"version":"crystal","text":"Once it has stored up enough heat, this POKéMON's body temperature can reach up to 1700 degrees."},{"version":"ruby","text":"FLAREON’s fluffy fur has a functional purpose - it releases heat into the air so that its body does not get excessively hot. This POKéMON’s body temperature can rise to a maximum of 1,650 degrees F."},{"version":"emerald","text":"FLAREON’s fluffy fur releases heat into the air so that its body does not get excessively hot. Its body temperature can rise to a maximum of 1,650 degrees F."},{"version":"firered","text":"It has a flame bag inside its body. After inhaling deeply, it blows out flames of nearly 3,100 degrees Fahrenheit."},{"version":"leafgreen","text":"When storing thermal energy in its body, its temperature can soar to over 1,600 degrees Fahrenheit."},{"version":"diamond","text":"It has a flame sac in its body. Its body temperature tops 1,650 degrees Fahrenheit before battle."},{"version":"platinum","text":"Inhaled air is heated in the flame sac in its body to an intense fire over 3,000 degrees Fahrenheit."},{"version":"heartgold","text":"It stores some of the air it inhales in its internal flame pouch, which heats it to over 3,000 degrees Fahrenheit."},{"version":"soulsilver","text":"It fluffs out its fur collar to cool down its body temperature, which can reach 1,650 degrees Fahrenheit."},{"version":"black-2","text":"Inhaled air is carried to its flame sac, heated, and exhaled as fire that reaches over 3,000 degrees F."},{"version":"y","text":"It has a flame bag inside its body. After inhaling deeply, it blows out flames of nearly 3,000 degrees Fahrenheit."},{"version":"omega-ruby","text":"Flareon’s fluffy fur has a functional purpose—it releases heat into the air so that its body does not get excessively hot. This Pokémon’s body temperature can rise to a maximum of 1,650 degrees Fahrenheit."},{"version":"sun","text":"When it catches prey or finds berries, it breathes fire on them until they’re well done, and then it gobbles them up."},{"version":"moon","text":"Its average body temperature is between 1,300 and 1,500 degrees Fahrenheit. In its internal flame sac, temperatures reach 3,000 degrees."},{"version":"ultra-sun","text":"If it inhales deeply, that’s a sign it’s about to attack. Prepare to be hit by flames of over 3,000 degrees Fahrenheit!"},{"version":"ultra-moon","text":"The flame chamber inside its body ignites when Flareon gets agitated, reaching temperatures of up to 1,650 degrees Fahrenheit."},{"version":"lets-go-pikachu","text":"It has a flame chamber inside its body. It inhales, then breathes out fire that is over 3,000 degrees Fahrenheit."},{"version":"sword","t